# =============================================================================
# What this repo IS: the source that produces the videos -- scripts, Remotion
# components, the gate suite, the skills, the docs.
#
# What this repo is NOT: the videos. Every rendered frame, master, audio file,
# b-roll clip and fetched screenshot is DERIVED and is excluded below. A clone
# of this repo regenerates them; it does not download them. The working tree is
# ~8.5 GB and almost all of that is output.
#
# GitHub hard-rejects any single file over 100 MB, and this tree contains a
# 452 MB wav, a 208 MB master and two mp4s over 100 MB. Those limits are the
# floor, not the reason -- the reason is that generated output does not belong
# in source control.
# =============================================================================

# --- secrets -----------------------------------------------------------------
# .env holds ELEVENLABS_API_KEY, ELEVENLABS_VOICE_ID and PEXELS_KEY.
# See README "Where the API keys go". NEVER commit this file.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
credentials.json
secrets.json

# --- identity / anonymity ----------------------------------------------------
# The channel is pseudonymous (CLAUDE.md hard rule 1). This file holds the
# creator's REAL identity strings so the anonymity gate can grep for them --
# publishing it would defeat the exact thing it protects.
#
# NOTE: git only treats '#' as a comment at the START of a line. Both patterns
# below used to carry trailing inline comments, which made them match nothing --
# so the identity file, and every fetched capture, were silently committable.
# Keep comments on their own lines.
capture/forbidden.json
capture/out/

# --- internal / private working material --------------------------------------
# Personal operating notes, channel strategy, topic pipeline and unpublished
# research. None of this is engine code and none of it is for public reading.
instructions-for-me/
startup-research/
claude gaurdrails/
channel-strategy.md
topic-research.md
GOALS.md
notes.md
skills-lock.json
make_tts_patch.py

# --- episode editorial content -----------------------------------------------
# This repo publishes the ENGINE, not the channel's writing. Scripts, narration,
# titles, descriptions and chapter lists are editorial content; excluding them
# also keeps the pseudonymous channel unlinked from this repo's author.
# The pipeline code, gates and components stay -- those are the technical work.
episodes/*/script.yaml
episodes/*/narration.txt
episodes/*/narration.draft.txt
episodes/*/packaging.md
episodes/*/notes.md
episodes/*/bench/
episodes/*/thumbnail/

# --- dependencies / build ----------------------------------------------------
node_modules
dist
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
*.zip

# --- rendered output ---------------------------------------------------------
# Matches any directory named `out` at any depth (episodes/*/out/, out/draft/).
out
out_*.mp4
*.mp4
*.mov
*.webm

# --- audio -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Narration masters, the ambient bed, and every synthetic SFX cue. The cues and
# the bed are REPRODUCIBLE: exact ffmpeg commands are in docs/research/
# sfx-palette.md and episodes/*/credits.md. Narration regenerates from
# script.yaml via make_tts.py.
*.wav
*.mp3
*.m4a
*.aac
*.raw
*.draft.mp3
narration.wav.json

# --- generated timing / caches -----------------------------------------------
# .tts_cache holds per-word alignment keyed by a hash of the beat text; it is
# rebuilt on the next make_tts.py run.
.tts_cache/
props.json
words.json

# timing.json is NOT ignored, despite being generated.
# `src/episodes.ts` imports it directly, so ignoring it means a fresh clone
# fails `tsc` on line 30 before it can do anything else -- a repo that does not
# typecheck out of the box is worse than one that ships a 4 KB generated file.
# It is small, carries no identity, and is the build input the registry needs.

# --- fetched media -----------------------------------------------------------
# Pexels b-roll and source screenshots. Licence-clean but not ours to
# redistribute; every one is credited with its URL in episodes/*/credits.md,
# so they are re-fetchable rather than vendored.
public/ep-*/
public/sfx/
assets/
assets-originals/
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
!docs/**/*.png

# --- local agent / editor state ----------------------------------------------
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
.claude/goal/
*.log
